  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44246198",
      "title": "Handling Errors",
      "sourceHash": "5cdd11a2913e7d25d6e8c1f701e823a2e8c1206ab005c57bca3da77c18b31695",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.19,
          "end": 4.86,
          "en": "So now with the use hook added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.86,
          "end": 9.12,
          "en": "and used here, we can also take this to the next level",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.12,
          "end": 11.16,
          "en": "by adding another new component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.16,
          "end": 12.99,
          "en": "which you also find attached.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.99,
          "end": 15.603,
          "en": "And that would be the ErrorBoundary component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.83,
          "end": 18.99,
          "en": "Now that's a type of component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.99,
          "end": 21.09,
          "en": "I covered earlier in the course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.09,
          "end": 23.58,
          "en": "in the class-based components section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.58,
          "end": 26.4,
          "en": "Because this component is built in a different way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.4,
          "end": 29.01,
          "en": "than all those other components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.01,
          "end": 31.17,
          "en": "It is built as a class that extends",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.17,
          "end": 34.17,
          "en": "the component class, which is provided by React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.17,
          "end": 37.62,
          "en": "And normally you wouldn't build components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.62,
          "end": 40.26,
          "en": "like this anymore, but this component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.26,
          "end": 43.38,
          "en": "this ErrorBoundary component must be built like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.38,
          "end": 47.431,
          "en": "because it uses some special error related React features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.431,
          "end": 51.9,
          "en": "that in the end allow you to catch errors that are thrown",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.9,
          "end": 56.79,
          "en": "by wrapped components and handle them in any way you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.79,
          "end": 59.712,
          "en": "You then have a render method here where you can define",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.712,
          "end": 63.723,
          "en": "what should be rendered on the screen if an error did occur.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.65,
          "end": 67.051,
          "en": "And I do cover this in greater detail",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.051,
          "end": 69.152,
          "en": "in that earlier course section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.152,
          "end": 73.35,
          "en": "where I do explore class-based components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.35,
          "end": 75.48,
          "en": "Here I'm providing this component to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.48,
          "end": 79.28999999999999,
          "en": "and you can use this ErrorBoundary to wrap it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.28999999999999,
          "end": 83.46000000000001,
          "en": "around this code that also uses suspense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.46000000000001,
          "end": 87.87,
          "en": "So ErrorBoundary here is wrapped around suspense and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 87.87,
          "end": 89.913,
          "en": "therefore also around UsePromiseDemo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 91.89,
          "end": 96.12,
          "en": "And if this component now would generate an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 96.12,
          "end": 99.363,
          "en": "because fetching the data fails, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 99.363,
          "end": 102.78,
          "en": "this ErrorBoundary would become active",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 102.78,
          "end": 105.483,
          "en": "and would show this output here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 106.35,
          "end": 109.11,
          "en": "An output where the error message is displayed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 109.11,
          "end": 112.77000000000001,
          "en": "and some fallback that can be passed as props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 112.77000000000001,
          "end": 115.65,
          "en": "to this ErrorBoundary component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 115.65,
          "end": 118.44,
          "en": "So this ErrorBoundary component is built such",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 118.44,
          "end": 121.08,
          "en": "that you can add a fallback prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 121.08,
          "end": 125.793,
          "en": "and the there we could say, something went wrong.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 127.11,
          "end": 129.18,
          "en": "And if you do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 129.18,
          "end": 133.53,
          "en": "and you then go to this promise that does the data fetching,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 133.53,
          "end": 136.98,
          "en": "and there, you accept this second parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 136.98,
          "end": 138.82,
          "en": "this reject parameter here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 139.95,
          "end": 142.38,
          "en": "so that you can reject the promise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 142.38,
          "end": 144.69,
          "en": "and therefore throw an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 144.69,
          "end": 147.3,
          "en": "If you do that and instead of resolving,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 147.3,
          "end": 150.12,
          "en": "you reject with a new error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 150.12,
          "end": 155.12,
          "en": "where I say, error, and you save that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 155.37,
          "end": 159.12,
          "en": "If you reload, you will see that error output here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 159.12,
          "end": 161.673,
          "en": "and that's coming from that ErrorBoundary.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 162.57,
          "end": 165.06,
          "en": "And I'm showing you this here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 165.06,
          "end": 168.84,
          "en": "not because ErrorBoundary would be a feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 168.84,
          "end": 173.16,
          "en": "that needs Next.js or some special project set up,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 173.16,
          "end": 174.66,
          "en": "that's not the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 174.66,
          "end": 178.74,
          "en": "ErrorBoundary components can be created in any React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 178.74,
          "end": 182.593,
          "en": "project, but I'm showing you this feature here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 182.593,
          "end": 187.593,
          "en": "because it is quite a nice combination if you have suspense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 187.68,
          "end": 190.203,
          "en": "and ErrorBoundary working together.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 191.04,
          "end": 194.25,
          "en": "Because with that setup here, you have a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 194.25,
          "end": 195.963,
          "en": "that handles the data fetching,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 197.25,
          "end": 200.793,
          "en": "then you have a component that handles the loading state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 201.69,
          "end": 203.85,
          "en": "and then you have a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 203.85,
          "end": 207.363,
          "en": "that shows an error if loading goes wrong.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 208.89,
          "end": 212.34,
          "en": "Now, when working with Next.js, you also have other ways",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 212.34,
          "end": 215.7,
          "en": "of handling errors as you learned in the previous section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 215.7,
          "end": 219.09,
          "en": "but this is an interesting pattern that you should be aware",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 219.09,
          "end": 223.07999999999998,
          "en": "of when using features like suspense and the use hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 223.07999999999998,
          "end": 226.143,
          "en": "or React server components and data fetching.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}